<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="011" project="spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r3">
  <metadata>
    <title>Default modules by user type + partner service-request switch (FR-19, FR-06 module half, #1568)</title>
    <phase>1 BFF auth and entitlement</phase>
    <gate>after 001 (A3 amendment approved)</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Tier-1 entitlement + Tier-2 record-set predicate (tags auth, bff-api)</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Authorization change on the shared external-access surface</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>C</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>001</deps>
    <tags>auth, bff-api, testing, config</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2-4 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Give workforce callers legal-front-door + policy-library and CIAM callers assigned-work by default, and add the per-customer partner switch that lets CIAM contacts use the Service Requests module (their own requests only).</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. ASP.NET Core and Dataverse authorization developer. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>ModuleEntitlementResolver returns default modules by principal type; ExternalAccess:PartnerServiceRequestsEnabled (default false) is bound; with it on, the service-requests descriptor's accessible set includes a CIAM contact's own requests and CIAM defaults add legal-front-door; tests cover both settings.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Owner 2026-10-09 option (b) and 2026-10-10 switch. Today ModuleEntitlementResolver.cs:44 OutsideCounselModules = { assigned-work } (also :79, :97) and workforce modules come only from sprk_approlemodulemap. The service-requests descriptor (Infrastructure/DI/ExternalAccessModule.cs:444-455, RecordEntity sprk_servicerequest, RecordIdAttribute sprk_requestedby) has AccessibleRecordIds predicate Plane == Workforce &amp;&amp; ContactId != Guid.Empty (:453). No ExternalAccess options class exists yet (only WorkforceIdentityOptions, section 'WorkforceIdentity').</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/ModuleEntitlementResolver.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/ExternalAccessModule.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/ExternalAccessOptions.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/appsettings.template.json</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/ModuleEntitlementResolverTests.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/WorkforceIdentityOptions.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Every route this task adds or modifies is mapped inside the /api/v1/external group (Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalAccessEndpoints.cs:60-63) so it inherits the ExternalCollaboration policy and CallerPrincipalAuthorizationFilter. No route in this task is mapped outside that group.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">No OBO on the external plane: every Dataverse and SPE call this task adds is app-only and scoped to the caller's accessible set (spec NFR-01).</constraint>
    <constraint source="bff-extensions">State the Placement Justification in the PR (cite .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md). Measure the publish-size delta against a fresh master build: more than +5 MB needs written justification; the total must stay at or under 60 MB. No new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Build only on the net10 SDK (10.0.1xx). Run /conflict-check before opening the PR: Api/ExternalAccess/** and Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/** are shared with unified-access-control-r2.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028 A3 (as amended by task 001)">Unentitled modules stay neither shown nor routable; this task changes only the default sets.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">sprk_approlemodulemap keeps adding optional extras on top of the defaults; it is never required for the defaults.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-010">Bind ExternalAccessOptions with the Options pattern in the existing ExternalAccessModule registration; no new DI module.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">With the switch off, behaviour for CIAM callers is exactly today's (0 service-request rows, module not entitled).</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Tier-1 module entitlement</topic>
    <files>
      <file>projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r3/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r3/spec.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/auth.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/auth/spaarke-sso-binding.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/auth/oauth-scopes.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</file>
      <file>docs/guides/auth-deployment-setup.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/api.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/api/endpoint-definition.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/api/endpoint-filters.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-001-minimal-api.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-008-endpoint-filters.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-010-di-minimalism.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/testing.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/testing/unit-test-structure.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/testing/mocking-patterns.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Load the knowledge files, read the relevant files listed above, declare rigor and model tier per task-execute Step 0.5.</step>
    <step order="1">Read ModuleEntitlementResolver.cs and its tests, and the service-requests descriptor in ExternalAccessModule.cs.</step>
    <step order="2">Add ExternalAccessOptions (section 'ExternalAccess', PartnerServiceRequestsEnabled bool, default false) and bind it.</step>
    <step order="3">Resolver: workforce principal (systemuser or workforce contact) → legal-front-door + policy-library + map extras; CIAM → assigned-work, plus legal-front-door when the switch is on.</step>
    <step order="4">Descriptor predicate: keep Workforce &amp;&amp; ContactId != Empty; when the switch is on, also allow CiamContact &amp;&amp; ContactId != Empty (still keyed by sprk_requestedby = the caller's contact).</step>
    <step order="5">Tests: each principal type with the switch off and on; a CIAM caller never gets another contact's request ids.</step>
    <step order="6">Seeding proof on the descriptor predicate: make it ignore the switch, confirm the switch-off CIAM test fails, restore.</step>
    <step order="7">Run `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` (0 errors) and `dotnet test tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/` (all pass); measure publish size per .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md and record it in the task notes.</step>
    <step order="8">Update tasks/TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` and this POML's &lt;status&gt; to completed; run `pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1`.</step>
    <step order="9">Record deviations, decisions and measurements in projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r3/notes/task-011-notes.md.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If a workforce systemuser caller has no ContactId on this code path (so the descriptor would return 0 rows for licensed staff), STOP and report — it changes whether licensed staff can see their requests.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>No ExternalAccess options class exists (grep 'SectionName' in Infrastructure/ExternalAccess finds only WorkforceIdentityOptions.cs:27).</existing>
    <extension>No: WorkforceIdentityOptions is the workforce member-test configuration; a module-availability switch is unrelated to the member test.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without a bound per-customer setting there is no way to turn partner service requests on for one customer (owner requirement 2026-10-10).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build and test the BFF</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Run shell commands</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/ModuleEntitlementResolver.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/ExternalAccessModule.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/ExternalAccessOptions.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/ModuleEntitlementResolverTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">A workforce systemuser caller is entitled to legal-front-door and policy-library with no sprk_approlemodulemap row.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A workforce contact caller is entitled to legal-front-door and policy-library.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A CIAM caller is entitled to assigned-work only when the switch is off, and to assigned-work + legal-front-door when it is on.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Map rows still add extra modules for workforce callers.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Switch off: a CIAM caller's service-requests accessible set is empty.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Switch on: a CIAM caller's service-requests accessible set contains only rows whose sprk_requestedby is that caller's contact.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The seeding proof is recorded in the task notes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Build is green; all unit tests pass; publish size is recorded and at or under 60 MB with no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the negative and edge cases named in these criteria. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in the task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-19, FR-06. Closes #1568 (module half).</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Before starting this task, load all files listed in &lt;knowledge&gt;&lt;files&gt;. Follow the task-execute skill for the mandatory pre-execution checklist.</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
